flowchart TB
    Q1{"S_pers > 0 ?<br/>beats the last observed value"}

    Q1 -->|no| N1["Do not deploy.<br/>Persistence is cheaper and better.<br/>Typical of high-inertia variables whose<br/>autocorrelation time exceeds the horizon."]
    Q1 -->|yes| Q2{"S_clim > 0 ?<br/>beats the seasonal cycle"}

    Q2 -->|no| N2["Seasonal artefact.<br/>The model has learned what month it is.<br/>Ship the climatology instead — it is cheaper<br/>to compute, cheaper to serve, and better.<br/>Invisible if only S_pers is reported."]
    Q2 -->|yes| Q3{"Does S_clim hold up<br/>as the horizon grows ?"}

    Q3 -->|"falls toward 0"| N3["Partly seasonal.<br/>Genuine skill at short range, decaying to a<br/>seasonal lookup at long range. Report the<br/>horizon at which it crosses."]
    Q3 -->|"stays positive"| N4["Genuine forecast skill.<br/>Information beyond both the present state<br/>and the seasonal cycle."]

    N4 --> Q4{"Does it transfer to<br/>a held-out site ?"}
    Q4 -->|no| N5["Interpolation, not transfer.<br/>Pooled metrics overstate what a user<br/>clicking unseen ocean will get.<br/>Restrict to trained sites, or say so."]
    Q4 -->|yes| N6["Deployable at arbitrary coordinates.<br/>Report the held-out figure, not the<br/>pooled one, as the expected skill."]

    classDef bad fill:#fdf0e6,stroke:#d1611f,stroke-width:2px,color:#1a1a1a
    classDef good fill:#e8eef5,stroke:#1f6fb2,stroke-width:2px,color:#1a1a1a
    class N1,N2,N5 bad
    class N4,N6 good
